CM_ "BMW E90 ABS/DSC module (Continental MK60E1, DSC81, software ZB 6769845A). Node DSC = this module. Every frame of the firmware's two message tables is listed with every field: fields the firmware discards and transmitted fields with a fixed value are included and say so. The application is the M3 MK60E5 software with features removed: layouts and fixed or discarded fields are read from this image, while meanings, scalings and DTC numbers are carried over from the M3 firmware where the handler matches and are not verified separately here. Not checked against a bus capture. Byte/bit numbering 0-based, little-endian (Intel). Bus: PT-CAN (powertrain CAN, 500 kbit/s). 0x0C8, 0x194, 0x1D6 and 0x2A6 are F-CAN frames the DSC forwards to this bus. The table's gateway record (ID 0x111) is the mailbox those frames go out through and is left out. This image has no CCP.";
CM_ BO_ 182 "Engine torque request from DSC to the engine ECU (BMW: Drehmomentanforderung DSC). Carries the ASR/MSR/AYC torque targets from traction control, with checksum and alive counter. Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 196 "Steering wheel angle relayed by DSC (BMW: Lenkradwinkel). The angle, rate and status come from the steering-angle sensor on F-CAN (0x0C8). No checksum or alive counter. Sent by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 206 "The four wheel speeds (BMW: Radgeschwindigkeit). Signed: negative while the wheel direction is known and backward. Magnitude limited to 300 km/h; 0 at or below the standstill threshold. The same frame is sent on F-CAN every 10 ms. Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 223 "Brake wheel-torque frame, in the place of the M3's 0x0E1. This firmware sends constants only (all fields not available); only the checksum and alive counter are live. Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 414 "Main DSC status frame (BMW: Status DSC): which control is active, ABS and DSC state, brake switch, brake applied, master-cylinder pressure. The alive counter steps once per 210 ms, not per frame. Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 416 "Vehicle speed, accelerations and yaw rate (BMW: Geschwindigkeit). Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 422 "Distance pulses (BMW: Wegstrecke): rolling wheel-sensor edge counters and the time they were counted over. A receiver takes the differences between frames. The counters restart on a distance reset. Sent by this module, every 100 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 690 "Wheel brake pressures, brake-pad wear stages and a slewed yaw rate. The hill-hold, brake pre-fill and disc-drying state fields of the M3 are fixed 0 here. Sent by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 797 "Flat-tyre indicator (RPA) state for the instrument cluster. Sent on request, as part of the reset handshake started by the RDC button (0x319 / 0x398). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 884 "Learned wheel (tyre) tolerance trims (BMW: Radtoleranzabgleich). Each value is the wheel's rolling-radius correction relative to the largest wheel, so in practice 0 or negative. The same frame is sent on F-CAN. Sent by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1193 "Network management frame of the DSC (OSEK-style NM, node 0x29; ID = 0x480 + node). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1449 "Check-control and service (CBS) messages to the instrument cluster, and frame requests. The meaning of bytes 3..7 depends on Kind. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1577 "Diagnostic response to the tester (KWP2000 over BMW's ISO-TP-like transport; DSC address 0x29, ID = 0x600 + address). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 200 "Steering-angle sensor frame from F-CAN (layout there). The DSC forwards a copy unchanged to this bus when its forward flag is set, so not every F-CAN frame appears here. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 404 "Cruise-control stalk. The DSC does not evaluate it; sent faster while the stalk is operated. Sent by the steering-column module (SZL) on F-CAN and forwarded unchanged to this bus by the DSC. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 470 "Steering-wheel audio and telephone buttons. The DSC does not evaluate them. Sent by the steering-column module (SZL) on F-CAN and forwarded unchanged to this bus by the DSC. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 678 "Wiper switch. Sent by the steering-column module (SZL) on F-CAN and forwarded unchanged to this bus by the DSC. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 168 "Engine ECU torque frame 1 (BMW: Drehmoment 1): delivered engine torque and engine status. Checksum and alive counter are supervised (15 or a repeated counter is an error); a timeout, alive or checksum error marks the values invalid and is reported as DTC D354. Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 169 "Engine ECU torque frame 2 (BMW: Drehmoment 2). Only the minimum (drag) torque is used; the other fields are read and discarded. Checksum and alive counter are supervised; errors are reported as DTC D355. Received by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 170 "Engine ECU torque frame 3 (BMW: Drehmoment 3): driver's torque demand, accelerator pedal, engine speed and pedal/cruise state. Checksum and alive counter are supervised; errors are reported as DTC D356. Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 186 "Gearbox data (BMW: Getriebedaten). Gear and gear-source flag are used, and only when a gearbox (automatic / DCT) is coded; the checksum (byte 5) and alive counter are supervised only then. Errors are reported as DTC D357. Used by AYC and TCS. Received by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 213 "Brake wheel-torque request from the cruise module (BMW: Anforderung Radmoment Bremse, DTC D35B). Received; every field is discarded and a timeout has no effect. Received by this module, every 20 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 304 "Terminal (ignition) status from the car access system (BMW: Klemmenstatus). The source of the ignition state; when it is missing the module falls back to its own terminal-15 input. Checksum and alive counter are supervised; errors are reported as DTC D35A. The frame is also forwarded unchanged to F-CAN. Received by this module, every 100 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 400 "Not in the M3's table; sender and meaning not established. Received; all three fields of its record are discarded and its timeout has no effect. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 419 "ACC long-term frame (DTC D35D). Received; the field is discarded. A timeout only sets a status flag. This image does not send the M3's 0x1A3. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 436 "Instrument cluster status (displayed speed, handbrake). Received; every field is discarded. Received by this module, every 100 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 550 "Rain sensor / wiper speed. Only the selection nibble is stored; it goes invalid after 40 s without the frame. Received by this module, every 10000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 740 "Trailer status from the trailer module (DTC D377 on timeout). Used by AYC trailer-sway logic and the flat-tyre monitor. Received by this module, every 5000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 784 "Outside temperature and relative time from the instrument cluster. Only the relative time is read (DTC D358 on timeout). Received by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 790 "DSC/DTC button from the junction box. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 793 "Tyre-pressure (RDC/RPA) reset button from the junction box. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 816 "Odometer, fuel level and range from the instrument cluster. Only the odometer is read. DTC D359 on timeout (50 s). Received by this module, every 10000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 896 "Vehicle identification number (last seven characters). Compared with the VIN stored in the module; the module can request the frame through 0x5A9. DTC D361 on timeout, 5E1D when invalid, 5E1F when it differs or the module is not initialised. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 904 "Vehicle type (BMW: Fahrzeugtyp). Received; every field is discarded. Received by this module, every 100 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 920 "Chassis settings from the iDrive controller (BMW: Bedienung Fahrwerk): DSC mode selection and the tyre-monitor reset. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 921 "M-Drive status. The 4-bit checksum and alive counter are checked, but both value fields are discarded on this image. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 944 "Reverse-gear status from the footwell module. Received; the field is discarded on this image. Received by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1152 "Network management frames of the other nodes. The module receives the whole range 0x480..0x4FF (sender node = ID - 0x480) through one masked mailbox; a DBC holds one message per ID, so only 0x480 is listed. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1408 "Service (condition-based service) answers. The module receives the range 0x580..0x5FF through one masked mailbox; a DBC holds one message per ID, so only 0x580 is listed. It uses the brake-pad answers: kinds 0x31 and 0x33 with item 2 (front) or 6 (rear). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1777 "Diagnostic request from the tester (KWP2000 over BMW's ISO-TP-like transport). The module accepts its own address 0x29 and the functional range 0xD0..0xEF. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ SG_ 182 Checksum "Checksum: sum of the other payload bytes plus the CAN ID, folded to 8 bits (s + (s >> 8)) & 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 182 AliveCounter "Alive counter, counts 0..14 and wraps; 15 is never sent.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TorqueTarget "Torque target (BMW: TORQ_TAR_DSC). Converted from the traction controller's 0.1 Nm request and clamped. With a single request this field carries it.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TorqueTarget_Adj "Second torque target (BMW: TORQ_TAR_ADJR_POS_DSC). With a single request it equals TorqueTarget.";
CM_ SG_ 182 RequestType "Kind of torque request (BMW: ST_TORQ_TAR_DSC). 3 is never sent.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteerAngle "Steering wheel angle: the F-CAN 0x0C8 angle multiplied by 0x405/1024 (x1.0049). 0.04395 deg per bit is the BMW figure; the firmware does not confirm it.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteerAngleStatus "Sensor status: 3 while the 0x0C8 status is flagged invalid, otherwise 0, 1 or 2 from the sensor's status class. The meanings of 1 and 2 are best guesses.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteerRate "Steering wheel angle rate, from the sensor's service data, same scaling as the angle.";
CM_ SG_ 196 Const_b40 "Fixed value 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 196 Const_b48 "Fixed value 1.";
CM_ SG_ 196 Const_b50 "Fixed value 0.";
CM_ SG_ 206 WheelSpeed_FL "Front-left wheel speed (wheel speed in 0.01 km/h x 4/25).";
CM_ SG_ 206 WheelSpeed_FR "Front-right wheel speed (wheel speed in 0.01 km/h x 4/25).";
CM_ SG_ 206 WheelSpeed_RL "Rear-left wheel speed (wheel speed in 0.01 km/h x 4/25).";
CM_ SG_ 206 WheelSpeed_RR "Rear-right wheel speed (wheel speed in 0.01 km/h x 4/25).";
CM_ SG_ 223 Checksum "Checksum: sum of the other payload bytes plus the CAN ID, folded to 8 bits (s + (s >> 8)) & 0xFF.";
