CM_ SG_ 1449 MessageId "Check-control message number (kind 0x40) or CBS item (kinds 0x30/0x32: 2 front pads, 6 rear pads). A frame request puts the requested CAN ID here high byte first (0x380 reads 0x8003).";
CM_ SG_ 1449 Byte3 "Check-control: bit 0 on, bits 5..2 repeat period, bits 7..6 a request field. CBS A: remaining range, low byte. CBS B: wear rate / 100 (0xFF unknown). Frame request: 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 1449 Byte4 "CBS A: remaining range, high byte (0x80 unknown). CBS B: 0. Otherwise 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 1449 Byte5 "CBS A: 0xF1. CBS B: 0xFE or 0xF0 plus the status. Otherwise 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 1449 Byte6 "CBS A: remaining percent (at most 100; 0xFE not valid, 0xFF unknown). CBS B: 0. Otherwise 0xFF.";
CM_ SG_ 1449 Byte7 "CBS A: pad replacement count (at most 30; 0xFF unknown). Otherwise 0xFF.";
